  814  As generative AI models proliferate, several important trends have emerged by 2026 that shape how these models are developed and utilized. The hottest models are now multimodal and integrated into broader systems, moving beyond single-purpose generation to "Generative World Models"internal simulators of environment dynamics that predict future states in compressed latent spaces. These models, such as those proposed by Fei-Fei Li's World Labs, aim to enable AI models to understand 3D environments and physical laws.
  815: World models utilize learned internal simulators to encode observations into dense embeddings and predict forward dynamics. By learning to compress environmental observations into a compact latent space, agents can train inside their own hallucinated "dreams"policies optimized against an imagined world and then transferred to the real one. However, this predictive power introduces a distinctive set of safety and security risks. World models produce imagined futures, meaning errors compound across multi-step rollouts in ways that single-inference models avoid.
